#version 460
// d4r engine, preset M: the reconstruction, written from the algorithm in M_NOTES.md. Every pixel resamples the
// frame's colour and the network's per-pixel outputs with the anisotropic Gaussians the network predicted for the
// 3x3 render texels around it, picks the two most likely of three motion candidates, fetches the previous result
// along them (bicubic) and blends it with the resampled colour.
//
// NGX ships two kernels with this exact body, differing only in the shared render-texel tile: rrlite_post_3_1
// (10x16, reconstruction/render >= 3) and rrlite_post_3_2 (15x27, 1.5 <= reconstruction/render < 3, sized for the
// worst case of its range, 1.5x). TILE_W/TILE_H select the tile for the engine's own 16x16-pixel block: 10x10
// covers reconstruction/render >= 3; 11x11 covers render/reconstruction <= 0.45 with jitter in [-0.5, 0.5];
// 15x15 covers the whole post_3_2 range (render/reconstruction <= 2/3).
//
// PRESET_L: preset L's rrlite_post_3_* (unfolded). The same body with two differences (L_NOTES.md): the Gaussians
